      "writtenOn": "2017-02-22T23:51:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"IBBR bit in BKUP_STS register reflects the violation to the VBAT voltage and the corruption to BBRM data \" - I expect this bit will be set if we try to read BBRAM after cutting VBAT, before we have re-written it. It\u0027s legitimate to return 0 there (we want BBRAM initialized to zero on VBAT failure). As for index bounds, we\u0027re handling them in the calling function I wrote. So I think this is ok.",
      "parentUuid": "845b9c36_d175d1f2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "bdce5ddaef58736fefd05df5d7565d7d1f5ef861",
