    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "109d93bb_bd8297bb",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-23T17:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still think we should return error code. index bound check should be done by the function and the caller just checks returned error to learn a boundary error. Assuming we use the prototype I proposed, you can still do:\n\nif (IS_BIT_SET(NPCX_BKUP_STS, NPCX_BKUP_STS_IBBR)) {\n    *value \u003d 0;\n    return EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n\nThis makes it more explicit that this is not an error but an expected valid case. Also, this makes it consistent with bbram_data_write.",
      "parentUuid": "fa9875ea_c056e073",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "bdce5ddaef58736fefd05df5d7565d7d1f5ef861",
